    {
        "content": "<p>A more serious issue is that there are duplicate definitions in Mathlib: Representation.subrepresentation (2022) and Representation.Subrepresentation (2025). </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/Basic.html#Representation.subrepresentation\">https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/Basic.html#Representation.subrepresentation</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/Subrepresentation.html#Subrepresentation\">https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/Subrepresentation.html#Subrepresentation</a></p>\n<p>The first <code>subrepresentation</code> passes it to an honest Representation, while the second <code>Subrepresentation</code> is a structure which is more primitive. My observation is that Representation.Subrepresentation.toRepresentation is the essentially same as Representation.subrepresentation. </p>\n<p>By the way, there does exist a lemma <code>Representation.subrepresentation_apply</code>, while I used the more primitive version <code>Subrepresentation</code>. Hopefully some expert could explain how to maintain such things.</p>",
        "id": 606631654,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1782446632
    }
]